## Source audit and change

- Java `ProcessQueue.putMessage` calls virtual `Message.getProperty(MAX_OFFSET)`
  on the final message in each insertion batch and uses its value to update
  `msgAccCnt`. Rust previously read the base message's property map directly.
- Added `MessageExtSubtype::property` and explicit `MessageExt::get_property` /
  `get_nullable_property` dispatch. The hook distinguishes no override from an
  explicit Java null and otherwise falls back to base properties.
- The Java custom subtype overrides only `MAX_OFFSET` to return
  `987654333` while its virtual queue offset is `987654321`. Java and Rust
  `ProcessQueue.putMessage` both report `msgAccCnt=12`; the fixture also
  compares the property getter invocation count, dispatch, message count,
  cached byte size and queue-tree key.
- Updated Phase 6, Phase 10 and Phase 18 compatibility records and the release
  checklist. This closes only the ProcessQueue backlog-accounting property
  read; other inherited virtual methods remain open.

